<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>document.getElementById("preview-container").style.display = "block";

// Preview rendering
{
  function text(id, content, json = true) {
    content = content.replaceAll("\\bullet", "\\\\\\quad\\bullet\\enspace");
    content = content.replaceAll("\\circ", "\\\\\\quad\\quad\\circ\\enspace");
    let block = "";
    block += "{\n";
    block += '\t"id": ' + id + ",\n";
    block += '\t"type": "text",\n';
    block += '\t"content": "' + content + '"\n';
    block += "}";
    return block;
  }

  function combine(lines, json = true) {
    lines = lines.split("\n");


    let blocks = "";
    let line = 0;
    let id = 1;
    let content;
    let texty;
    let definition;
    let url;
    let src;
    let alt;


    while (true) {
      if (line &gt;= lines.length) {
        break;
      }
      switch (lines[line]) {
        case "text":
          if (blocks) {
            blocks += ",\n";
          }
          line += 1;
          if (lines[line]) {
            content = lines[line]?.replace("\n", "");
          } else {
            content = "";
          }
          blocks += text(id, content, json);
          id += 1;
          line += 1;
          break;
        case "":
          line += 1;
          break;
        default:
          console.debug("Unknown type encountered: " + lines[line]);
          line += 1;
          // return "[\n" + blocks + "\n]";
      }
    }


    // JSON.parse("[\n" + blocks + "\n]");


    return "[\n" + blocks + "\n]";
  }

  async function renderSolution(solution) {
    document.getElementById("preview").replaceChildren();
    {
      const p = document.createElement("p");
      p.innerHTML = "Solution 1:";
      p.style.fontWeight = "bold";
      p.style.fontStyle = "italic";
      p.style.marginTop = "0";
      p.style.marginBottom = ".5rem";
      document.getElementById("preview").appendChild(p);
    }


    solution = JSON.parse(solution);


    let paragraph = null;

    function ensureParagraph() {
      if (!paragraph) {
        paragraph = document.createElement("p");
        paragraph.style.marginTop = ".5rem";
        paragraph.style.marginBottom = ".5rem";
        document.getElementById("preview").appendChild(paragraph);
      }
    }


    for (const block of solution) {
      switch (block.type) {
        case "text":
          ensureParagraph();
          paragraph.append(block.content);
          break;
      }
    }
    if (paragraph) {
      render(paragraph);
    }
  }

  function render(element) {
    renderMathInElement(element, {
      delimiters: [{
          left: "$$",
          right: "$$",
          display: true
        },
        {
          left: "$",
          right: "$",
          display: false
        },
      ],


      ignoredTags: ["script", "noscript", "style", "textarea", "pre", "code"],


      throwOnError: false,


      macros: {
        "\\EE": "\\mathbb{E}",
      },
    });
  }
  async function renderSolutionFormat(event) {
    const text = document.getElementById("text-editor").value;
    const solution = combine(text, false).replaceAll("\\", "\\\\");


    // to see unredered output, uncomment below line and comment the line below it
    // document.getElementById("preview").innerText = solution;
    renderSolution(solution);
  }
  const textEditor = document.getElementById("text-editor");
  textEditor.addEventListener("input", renderSolutionFormat);
  // set the initial value that causes the overflowing:

  document.getElementById("text-editor").value = String.raw`text
    This problem is all about translating English into math. To begin, we know $k$ is $m$ percent of $n$. Knowing that $x\%$ of anything is just $\frac{x}{100}$ times that value, if $k$ is $m$ percent of $n$, then $k=\frac{m}{100}\cdot n$. From here, knowing that some percent of $m$ is $nk$, we contruct the second equation: $nk=\frac{x}{100}\cdot m$, where $x$ is the unknown. Now we have a system of two equations. Substituting $k$ in the second equation with the first equation, we get:$\\ \quad\bullet \enspace (\frac{m}{100}\cdot n)n=\frac{x}{100}\cdot m$ | Original equation$\\ \quad \bullet \enspace \frac{mn^2}{100}=\frac{xm}{100}$ | Combining terms$\\\quad\bullet\enspace n^2=x$ | Multiplying both sides by $\frac{100}{m}$ to solve for $x\\$Thus, $m$ is $n^2\%$ of $nk$. To see this, below are some example values:$\\\begin{array}{|l|l|l|l|l|}\hline k &amp; m &amp; n &amp; n^2 &amp; nk \\ \hline 30 &amp; 300 &amp; 10 &amp; 100 &amp; 300 \\ \hline 20 &amp; 100 &amp; 20 &amp; 400 &amp; 400 \\ \hline 10 &amp; 10 &amp; 100 &amp; 10000 &amp; 1000 \\ \hline 1 &amp; 20 &amp; 5 &amp; 25 &amp; 5 \\ \hline \end{array}\\$During the competition, it may be worth it to check if your answer is correct using values for $k$, $m$, and $n$. However, more than one check is not really necessary. Nonetheless, we can see our answer is correct: $n^2$.`;
  renderSolutionFormat();
}</code></pre>
